[center][img]https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/ReidenXerx/fo4-overture@bf3c5a656744651ec61f7b883b2889c978587075/docs/img/divider.png[/img][/center]

[size=5][b][color=#ff6b8b]What it is[/color][/b][/size]

Overture is a conversation. Talk to an adult stranger and, once a day, it opens with them before their own dialogue: no hotkey, no menu, no spell. Pick your words, read how they take it, and if you read them right and pick the right place, they may say yes. It is built on [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/mods/109219]Rapport[/url], which keeps what your words did as the bond between you, and runs the scene if you let it.

[size=5][b][color=#ff6b8b]Four ways to try[/color][/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Offer[/b]: caps, a gift, something material.
[*][b]Charm[/b]: fancy words, patience, a compliment.
[*][b]Blunt[/b]: crude, direct, explicit.
[*][b]Linger[/b]: say little, stay, be present.
[/list]

Every NPC is one of four kinds of people, and each way lands with exactly one of them. The game never says who is which: you learn it from how they answer. [b]The place matters too:[/b] a blunt line in a crowded room recoils, even on the one person who would have liked it somewhere else.

[center][img]https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/ReidenXerx/fo4-overture@bf3c5a656744651ec61f7b883b2889c978587075/docs/img/flow.jpg[/img][/center]

[center][img]https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/ReidenXerx/fo4-overture@bf3c5a656744651ec61f7b883b2889c978587075/docs/img/conversation.jpg[/img][/center]

A line that lands opens the next wheel and brings you closer; a miss ends it for the day, and an intimate line in a crowded room makes them recoil.

[size=5][b][color=#ff6b8b]What you get[/color][/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Every line is voiced.[/b] 196 NPC lines in 11 voices, 4,749 voice files. Characters with their own actor answer in the closest voice we have, through Rapport, for that line only.
[*][b]You speak too,[/b] in one of two voices designed for this mod, a woman's and a man's, never a copy of any actor. Every option on the wheel comes in five versions, and each conversation picks one, so the same choice doesn't always read or sound the same (built, not yet seen in game).
[*][b]A narrator, not a scoreboard.[/b] After each conversation, one line says what your words did and hints at what to try: another way, another day, somewhere private, after dark. It never names their type.
[*][b]"Not now" and "not here" are not a no.[/b] Ask again later the same day, or find them somewhere quiet, and it picks up at the question.
[*][b]Names for the nameless.[/b] Talk to a Settler or a Drifter and they get a real name, the same one every time you load.
[*][b]Lovers.[/b] Close enough and after a scene together, you are a couple to everyone. Other people treat them as taken, and your other lovers notice when you are with someone else: some are hurt, some are thrilled.
[*][b]Orientation is real.[/b] Some people are simply not into your sex. No words and no time will change that, and the narrator tells you so, so you stop trying.
[*][b]Companions[/b] have a system of their own: days together, fights survived and their own affinity bring you closer, and a companion who wants you may find a moment to say so. You can ask them for a moment too. Works with any companion built on the game's own companion system, and with Amazing Follower Tweaks.
[/list]

[center][img]https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/ReidenXerx/fo4-overture@bf3c5a656744651ec61f7b883b2889c978587075/docs/img/voiced.jpg[/img][/center]

Both sides of every conversation are spoken: 11 voices for the people you approach, two of your own, 4,749 files in all.

[center][img]https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/ReidenXerx/fo4-overture@bf3c5a656744651ec61f7b883b2889c978587075/docs/img/divider.png[/img][/center]

[size=5][b][color=#ff6b8b]Before you play[/color][/b][/size]

[quote]
[b]"A yes starts a scene" is off by default.[/b] Out of the box, a yes is only a yes: the conversation, the voices, the bond and the narrator all work, and nothing starts. Switch it on in MCM to have Rapport start the scene. It is off because a Rapport scene with the player in it has not been run in a real game yet, and we would rather you choose it knowing that.

[b]Nothing starts until you leave Vault 111.[/b] No scene and no approach during the game's opening, from character creation to the vault door; alternate starts and MS Skip Prewar Sanctuary work as expected. Using an unusual alternate start that never finishes the opening? MCM, first page, [i]Start now[/i]. [i]Start now[/i] needs Rapport 0.2.2.

[b]Keep the voice files loose.[/b] Don't pack Overture's [font=Courier New]Sound\Voice\Overture.esp[/font] into an archive. Rapport finds a missing recording by looking for the loose file, so packed lines go silent or borrow the wrong voice.

[b]Needs:[/b] Fallout 4 1.10.163 with F4SE, [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/mods/109219]Rapport 0.2.1[/url] or newer, [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/mods/27216]Extended Dialogue Interface[/url] and [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/mods/31304]AAF[/url]. MCM is optional. With an older Rapport, Overture still runs, without names, lovers or the narrator, and says so once.
[/quote]

[size=5][b][color=#ff6b8b]FAQ[/color][/b][/size]

[b]What has been tested in game?[/b]
[spoiler]Checked in game: talking to people, the four ways to try with every kind of person in public and private rooms, the bond each step writes, every answer to the question (with the verdict set by hand), the narrator's line and names for the nameless. Built but not yet run in a real game: the answer decided live from start to finish, "not now" and "not here" reopening, lovers and jealousy, scenes with you, the whole companion module including "Ask for a moment", lip sync, and the wheel's five versions showing up. The owner is leaving those to the community, so please tell us what you see, good or bad. The sticky post keeps the list current.[/spoiler]

[b]Who can I talk to?[/b]
[spoiler]Adult humans and ghouls, once each per game day. Not anyone who has ever been a companion, who has the companion system instead; not anyone in combat or busy in a scene of their own; not a gen-1 or gen-2 synth.[/spoiler]

[b]Why won't Ivy offer "Ask for a moment"?[/b]
[spoiler]On purpose. Ivy keeps her own route ("Let's make love."), and Overture turns her fade to black into a real Rapport scene when "A yes starts a scene" is on, then hands her back to her own story.[/spoiler]

[b]Is it explicit?[/b]
[spoiler]The crude kind of person talks dirty, on purpose: swearing, teasing, specifically filthy. Everything is between adults and wanted by both. It is an 18+ mod.[/spoiler]

[b]Where is every setting explained?[/b]
[spoiler]In the sticky posts: every MCM setting, what each word is worth, the companion system, and the debug buttons.[/spoiler]

